From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:25:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/15] payload: hand an inline payload a live ANS session on
 the T8132

U-Boot adopts the post-M4 ANS session instead of starting ANS (its
apple_nvme_adopt() sends no RTKit handshake), but on a Mach-O boot the
aura Stage 1 that read this stage leaves ANS quiesced. An inline U-Boot
payload then finds no disk. Bring ANS up on the T8132 before the
hand-off and keep it running, as for Linux from boot=.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 src/payload.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/payload.c b/src/payload.c
index 268be9e7..52fee20d 100644
--- a/src/payload.c
+++ b/src/payload.c
@@ -529,6 +529,18 @@ int payload_run(void)
          * link back up, and kboot_prepare_dt() passes the SART entries on.
          */
         nvme_keep_running_for_linux = boot_spec != NULL;
+        /*
+         * T8132: U-Boot adopts the post-M4 ANS session instead of starting ANS, and an
+         * aura Stage 1 leaves it quiesced after reading this stage. Bring it up and hand
+         * the inline payload a live, enabled session, as for Linux from boot=.
+         */
+        if (!boot_spec && chip_id == T8132) {
+            if (!nvme_init()) {
+                printf("Payload: cannot prepare the T8132 ANS session for the payload\n");
+                goto boot_failed;
+            }
+            nvme_keep_running_for_linux = true;
+        }
         if (!boot_spec && !nvme_shutdown())
             goto boot_failed;
         cpufreq_init();
